  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Palestinian Civil Society and Inclusion Project.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Palestinian Civil Society and Inclusion (PCSI-I) project will work to strengthening the role of Palestinian civil society organisations to oversee governance and service delivery by the Palestinian Authority and other local duty bearers and hold them to account. PCSI will also work for greater empowerment and inclusion of women and will reach to areas of most marginalised groups. The project will be delivered through an Accountable Grant Arrangement with AMAN Coalition for Integrity and Accountability. AMAN is a leading non-governmental, not-for-profit civil society organisation and is the national chapter of Transparency International in Palestine and focuses on combating corruption and enhance the values of integrity, the principles of transparency and the systems of accountability (ITA) in Palestinian society.  

The overall objective of the project responds well to the declining context of PA&#x2019; legitimacy, lack of citizen&#x2019; trust, and weak state&#x2019; accountability platforms to hold the executive to account. The outcomes include. 
Outcome 1: Increased adoption by decision-makers of public policies that protect civic space.
Outcome 2: Enhanced community engagement in policy making and holding power to account for the common good. 
Outcome 3: Greater empowerment and inclusion of women in combating gendered corruption and in holding power to account.</narrative>
  </description>
